{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1779898553,"nonce":"wLXTNFeJwm8Sju4fm8FWG9XQgZM=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDj3yO88AAAAGDyVIxQ"},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1779898553,"nonce":"XALwmf0aXYa28S8JJAlnaOV2zbI=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDj3yO88AAAAGDyVKqQ"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779980479,"nonce":"/dPRPpCvJ+Eq+kjr5DUazegP1Vk=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEB6D-w","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/186#issuecomment-4565402619"},"message":"## Process note — testing `/start-deployment` skill (workspace #501)\n\nThis deployment will be the **first end-to-end trial** of the new workspace `/start-deployment` skill ([ros2_agent_workspace#501](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace/issues/501) / [ADR-0014](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace/blob/main/docs/decisions/0014-deployment-mode.md), merged 2026-05-28). The skill replaces the manual deployment-start steps and loads the urgency contract (sterile cockpit / mitigate-before-diagnose / time-box) into the agent session.\n\n**Prerequisite:** [unh_echoboats_project11#194](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/194) must be merged on `jazzy` first — that lands `.agents/deployment.yaml` (which the skill stops without) and the shrunk `docs/logs/README.md` that points at the workspace docs.\n\n### Log meta-observations during the deployment\n\nIn addition to the normal mission content, every host log should capture **observations about the skill itself** — this is a trial run, and the feedback loops back into the skill's v2 design. Worth noting:\n\n- **Where the skill helped** (cycle-time savings, contract kept you on-task, three-state detection routed correctly).\n- **Where the skill stumbled** (any step that needed manual fallback, any wrong assumption from `.agents/deployment.yaml`, prompts the operator hit, anything that felt clunky).\n- **Field-side `issue_sync` behavior** — first run of the git-bug + gitcloud commands in production. Note `field_pull` / `field_list_open` / `field_show` timing and any hiccups; this is what makes field-side three-state detection work.\n- **Contract adherence** — when sterile-cockpit / mitigate-before-diagnose bit, when it relaxed at wrap-up. If the agent rabbit-holed or skipped the contract, log when and why.\n- **Pre-flight format** — tides in metres, explicit TZ. Note if NOAA / NWS lookups against the configured stations (Fort Point 8423898, Clark Island ACT0731, NWS GYX) returned what was expected.\n\nThese observations belong inline in the per-host logs alongside the normal entries — separate `## Skill trial notes` section per log isn't needed; just tag relevant lines with `[start-deployment trial]` so they're greppable for the post-deployment writeup.\n\n### After the deployment\n\nWrap-up should include a follow-up issue on `ros2_agent_workspace` capturing the v2 candidates surfaced during this trial — separate from the carry-forward operational issues filed against this repo.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}